  "createmetallurgy.ponder.casting_blocks.header": "Casting Molten Metals",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.casting_blocks.text_1": "Casting Blocks can be used to cool down Molten Metals into a specific shape",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.casting_blocks.text_2": "The Casting Basin is used to cast up to a entire block",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.casting_blocks.text_3": "While the Casting Table is used to cast Items using Graphite Molds",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.casting_blocks.text_4": "Molds can be locked in place using the lock mode selection slot",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.casting_blocks.text_5": "If you are using Funnels while keeping the mold unlocked...",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.casting_blocks.text_6": "...you might need a Brass Funnel to not extract Molds",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.header": "Setting up a Foundry",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.text_1": "Industrial Crucibles can also be used as bigger Foundry Basin",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.text_2": "You can add or remove attachments like Gauges any time and anywhere using a Wrench",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.text_3": "To melt metals, you will need to heat up the Foundry...",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.text_4": "...Crucibles must have a base size of 5x5 blocks to reach the maximum temperature",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.text_5": "However, each base block without a burner below it will cool down the Crucible. Higher heat means faster melting!",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.text_6": "Unlike Foundry Basins, Crucibles are large enough to melt down bigger items and several at once",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.text_7": "The current heat of the Crucibles can be inspected with Engineer's Goggles and reported in Thermal Units (Tu)",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.text_8": "Items can also be transferred on each side like an Item Vault, same for fluids like a Fluid Tank",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry.text_9": "Crucibles can also perform other types of recipes, such as entity melting and alloying",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_basin.header": "Melting Metals with Foundry Basin",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_basin.text_1": "The Foundry Basin is comparable to a classic Basin...",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_basin.text_2": "...However, it can only hold 9 Items of the same type",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_basin.text_3": "Put a Foundry Lid on top, and your Foundry is now ready!",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_basin.text_4": "Like the Basin, a Faucet can extract recipes Items...",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_basin.text_5": "...and Fluids with a Item Drain",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_basin.text_6": "Make sure to close the Foundry Top else the recipe won't start",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_mixer.header": "Making Alloys with Foundry Mixer",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_mixer.text_1": "The Foundry Mixer is similar to the Mechanical Mixer...",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_mixer.text_2": "...However, it has a much higher stress impact",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_mixer.text_3": "With a Glassed Foundry Top between them, you will be able to make alloys",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_mixer.text_4": "In order to keep molten metals warm enough...",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_mixer.text_5": "...you will need a Heated Blaze Burner",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_mixer.text_6": "Make sure to close the Foundry Top else the recipe won't start",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_mixer.text_7": "If you are using Fluid Pipes instead of a Item Drain...",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.foundry_mixer.text_8": "...you might use a Smart Fluid Pipe, to avoid pumping out un-processed Fluids",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.industrial_crucible.header": "Build up Industrial Crucible",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.industrial_crucible.text_1": "Industrial Crucibles can be used to store molten metals",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.industrial_crucible.text_2": "You can add windows with a Wrench!",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.industrial_crucible.text_3": "Crucibles can also store multiple fluids at the same time!",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.light_bulbs.header": "Using Light Bulbs",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.light_bulbs.text_1": "Light Bulbs are an alternative light source to the Redstone Lamp",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.light_bulbs.text_2": "They emit light proportionally to the strength of the Redstone signal received",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.light_bulbs.text_3": "Light Bulbs are available in all colors",
  "createmetallurgy.ponder.light_bulbs.text_4": "Placing items in Address slot can connect others light bulbs in a Network",
